The `.yarnrc.yml` exclusion guard inside `findMock.up.mockImplementation` is duplicated verbatim in two modified test cases (this one and the `'when multiple lockfiles are in a project, prefers yarn'` test around line 228). Consider extracting a shared helper, for example:

```ts
function makeRealFindExcludingYarnrc(realFind: typeof import('empathic/find')) {
  return (filename: unknown, opts?: unknown) => {
    if (typeof filename === 'string' && filename === '.yarnrc.yml') return undefined;
    return (realFind.up as any)(filename, opts);
  };
}
```
This removes the need to keep both copies in sync if the exclusion logic ever changes.

The new `getYarnVersionFromPackageJson` function returns `1` when `match[1] === '1'` (i.e., `packageManager: 'yarn@1.x'` in `package.json`), which causes `getYarnVersion` to return `1` and ultimately yield `Yarn1Proxy`. This branch has no test coverage. A regression that made the function return `2` for `yarn@1.x` (e.g., an off-by-one in the regex capture group check) would go undetected. Please add a test such as:

```ts
it('YARN1 VIA packageManager FIELD: when package.json has packageManager yarn@1.22.4', () => {
  // set up yarn.lock found, package.json found, packageManager: 'yarn@1.22.4'
  // ...
  expect(JsPackageManagerFactory.getPackageManager()).toBeInstanceOf(Yarn1Proxy);
});
```
